## Summary

Delivered a production-grade, native Apple-idiomatic **`SettingsSearch`** feature view (P4 · 0215) at full parity with `features/settings/components/SettingsSearch.tsx`, committed as `0c8b8e53` (14 files, 2844 lines).

**What was built** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/SettingsSearch.*`):
- **Data parity** — verbatim port of `getSettingsIndex` (all 53 entries: ids, hrefs, sections, i18n keys, keywords) split across 3 catalog files, plus `searchSettings` scoring tiers (1000→100), `fuzzyMatch`, `MAX_RESULTS=8` cap, and a stable catalog-order tiebreak.
- **Composition** — SwiftUI combobox: search field + inline results panel, Arrow↑/↓ wrap-around, Enter commits the highlight, Escape clears, hover-activates rows; commit parses `entry.href` into `{path, fragment}` delegated to the host via `onSelect` (web `navigate`).
- **Every state renders** — idle / loading / content / empty (`No matching settings.`) / error, plus the orthogonal live / stale (chip + one-shot auto-refresh) / offline freshness axis.
- **Architecture** — bound through a P1/S8 source seam (no HTTP in the view), P1/S10 i18n facade, P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry; VoiceOver labels/traits on every control, Dynamic Type, reduce-motion. Tests: scoring/catalog/destination/projector/nav/a11y + state-holder (XCTest).

**Verification** (all host-runnable gates green): `swiftlint --strict` 0 violations · `swiftformat --lint` 0 · placeholder gate COUNT=0 (1 sanctioned `parity:allow` for the verbatim web key) · isolated SwiftPM build under **Swift 6 strict concurrency** clean · **75/75 logic checks pass** · `xcodegen generate` enumerates all 14 members.

**Honest status — `STATUS=BLOCKED`** (logged with API evidence): the full-app `xcodebuild … build test` is **unrunnable on this runner** — Command Line Tools only (no Xcode), no iOS SDK/Simulator runtime, no iPhone 16 sim, no Gradle/KMP to stage `Shared.xcframework`. This is the identical macOS-pending deferral already recorded for ToolCard / AlertMessageEditor / FSMTimelineChart and is deferred to the `macos-latest` acceptance runner. The surface itself is complete and green on every gate that can run here.

